{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"S3CloudFileSystem"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This backend requires the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AWSS3"},{"type":"text","text":" product from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/awslabs\/aws-sdk-swift","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". With the source distribution,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enable the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"S3"},{"type":"text","text":" package trait and SPM resolves it automatically. With the binary distribution"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(XCFrameworks), add aws-sdk-swift as a separate package dependency in your project."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"S3 is a flat key-value store, not a hierarchical file system. This backend","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simulates directory semantics using key prefixes and ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" delimiters — the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard S3 convention. For example, the Ensembles path","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ensembleId\/events\/data.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" maps to the S3 key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"<keyPrefix>ensembleId\/events\/data.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Directory creation writes a zero-byte marker object with a trailing ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" key.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Directory listing uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"ListObjectsV2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a delimiter to discover","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"“subdirectories” via common prefixes. This approach is compatible with S3","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"console browsing and third-party tools.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The app configures an ","type":"text"},{"code":"S3Client","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with its own credentials and injects it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at init time:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let s3Client = try await S3Client()","let cloudFS = S3CloudFileSystem(","    client: s3Client,","    bucketName: \"my-bucket\",","    keyPrefix: \"ensembles\/\"",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Authentication","level":2,"anchor":"Authentication"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The AWS SDK for Swift resolves credentials automatically from the standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"credential provider chain. Configure credentials using any of:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Environment variables"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and optionally ","type":"text"},{"code":"AWS_SESSION_TOKEN","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Shared credentials file","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"~\/.aws\/credentials","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (set via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aws configure"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"ty